Date: Mon, 7 Sep 2026 22:07:35 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1279/3799] soh: rename func_800425B0 -> WaterBox_GetSurface3

Name source: DEDUCED from the code (confidence HIGH) -- zeldaret/oot
leaves this symbol address-named too, so there is no upstream name to adopt.
Reason: its doc comment says it is the "same as WaterBox_GetSurfaceImpl, but tests if WaterBox properties & 0x80000 != 0". It joins the file's existing WaterBox_GetSurface1 / WaterBox_GetSurface2 / WaterBox_GetSurfaceImpl family as the third numbered variant; nothing calls it.
Defined in soh/src/code/z_bgcheck.c.

Tagged [LLM:HIGH] at the definition, every declaration and every call site, so a
reader meeting the name anywhere knows it is inferred.
---
 soh/src/code/z_bgcheck.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/soh/src/code/z_bgcheck.c b/soh/src/code/z_bgcheck.c
index 995bc954d..2e95e142e 100644
--- a/soh/src/code/z_bgcheck.c
+++ b/soh/src/code/z_bgcheck.c
@@ -4355,7 +4355,8 @@ u32 WaterBox_GetLightSettingIndex(CollisionContext* colCtx, WaterBox* waterBox)
  * returns true if point is within the xz boundaries of an active water box, else false
  * `ySurface` returns the water box's surface, while `outWaterBox` returns a pointer to the WaterBox
  */
-s32 func_800425B0(PlayState* play, CollisionContext* colCtx, f32 x, f32 z, f32* ySurface, WaterBox** outWaterBox) {
+// LLM generated name (HIGH), was func_800425B0: its doc comment says it is the "same as WaterBox_GetSurfaceImpl, but tests if WaterBox properties & 0x80000 != 0". It joins the file's existing WaterBox_GetSurface1 / WaterBox_GetSurface2 / WaterBox_GetSurfaceImpl family as the third numbered variant; nothing calls it.
+s32 WaterBox_GetSurface3(PlayState* play, CollisionContext* colCtx, f32 x, f32 z, f32* ySurface, WaterBox** outWaterBox) {
     CollisionHeader* colHeader = colCtx->colHeader;
     u32 room;
     WaterBox* curWaterBox;
